1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,070
Characters, actions, places, occupations,
and events in this series

2
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:08,750
are fictional and created
for entertainment purposes only.

3
00:00:08,790 --> 00:00:13,280
They are not intended to urge
or promote any behavior in the series.

4
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:15,720
Viewer discretion is advised.

5
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:18,040
We've always stuck together lately.

6
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:19,680
Then you two should spend some time apart.

7
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:21,270
Chan, you know
what you need to do, right?

8
00:00:21,310 --> 00:00:23,050
There’s nothing
I need to worry about, right?

9
00:00:23,230 --> 00:00:24,920
About your mom,

10
00:00:25,050 --> 00:00:27,040
she is the real last boss, like Sun said.

11
00:00:27,470 --> 00:00:28,400
You are sick?

12
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:30,570
I want someone
to take care of me right now.

13
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:32,009
You want me to stay and take care of you?

14
00:00:34,340 --> 00:00:36,450
Does it suit your palate, Mom?

15
00:00:36,730 --> 00:00:39,770
But I believe that you can win her over.

16
00:00:39,990 --> 00:00:42,250
We are only going to take
our hatred out on each other.

17
00:00:42,370 --> 00:00:43,690
Don’t you feel sorry for Chan?

18
00:00:43,850 --> 00:00:46,440
Why do we have to hate each other?

19
00:00:52,490 --> 00:00:53,450
Mom.

20
00:00:56,090 --> 00:00:57,400
I love you.

21
00:00:58,990 --> 00:01:01,040
I invited you to join me today.

22
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:03,580
Because I want you…

23
00:01:05,120 --> 00:01:07,680
to be present
in the most important moment of my life.

24
00:01:50,310 --> 00:01:52,300
I will use these earrings

25
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:55,900
to propose to you.

26
00:01:58,310 --> 00:01:59,850
My proposal is simple.

27
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:01,900
It’s nothing special.

28
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:04,900
I didn’t throw a big event

29
00:02:05,870 --> 00:02:07,180
like I always do.

30
00:02:16,250 --> 00:02:18,100
I just want to show you

31
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:23,400
that I’m doing this
out of my genuine love.

32
00:02:31,570 --> 00:02:33,300
We don’t need a grand gesture

33
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:38,900
or an extravagant event.

34
00:02:44,210 --> 00:02:46,300
I will use these earrings

35
00:02:48,590 --> 00:02:50,200
to propose to you.

36
00:02:58,490 --> 00:03:00,170
Will you marry me, Key?

37
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:45,800
Thank you.

38
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:07,490
Don’t you think this is too much?

39
00:05:08,350 --> 00:05:10,550
You fired Key’s band from the bar.

40
00:05:11,440 --> 00:05:13,130
Just because she’s my fiancée.

41
00:05:14,610 --> 00:05:15,900
I already made up my mind.

42
00:05:16,190 --> 00:05:17,800
I also found a new band.

43
00:05:21,690 --> 00:05:22,700
Mrs. Chanya.

44
00:05:23,070 --> 00:05:25,420
Miss Key’s band is very popular.

45
00:05:25,460 --> 00:05:26,330
So what?

46
00:05:27,300 --> 00:05:29,350
The new band is also talented.

47
00:05:30,270 --> 00:05:31,800
They have their fan base.

48
00:05:32,170 --> 00:05:34,350
Are you sure you’re going to do this?

49
00:05:34,730 --> 00:05:36,540
I’m doing this for our hotel’s interests.

50
00:05:37,530 --> 00:05:38,500
It’s not true.

51
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:41,270
You’re not doing this for the hotel.

52
00:05:42,490 --> 00:05:45,000
You’re doing this to pressure me.

53
00:05:53,070 --> 00:05:54,270
It’s okay, Chan.

54
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:57,270
That’s enough.

55
00:05:59,090 --> 00:06:00,500
I’m sorry, Key.

56
00:06:01,420 --> 00:06:03,920
This is not fair to you
and your bandmates.

57
00:06:06,590 --> 00:06:08,520
They won’t have a problem with it.

58
00:06:16,590 --> 00:06:21,000
You’re not going to get your way with us
by doing this.

59
00:06:22,650 --> 00:06:24,320
I’m doing everything for you.

60
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:28,410
When will you understand
that she is not a good match for you?

61
00:06:30,150 --> 00:06:34,000
Who gets to decide who is right for me?

62
00:06:35,750 --> 00:06:37,500
Only your opinion matters?

63
00:06:39,710 --> 00:06:41,100
My partner,

64
00:06:42,550 --> 00:06:44,600
I can’t even choose that myself?

65
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:47,800
Do you love her more than me, Chan?

66
00:06:48,500 --> 00:06:49,690
Why are you so against me?

67
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:51,000
Mom.

68
00:06:59,120 --> 00:07:00,950
You’ve changed since you met Key.

69
00:07:02,300 --> 00:07:04,170
You are not the same daughter
I used to know.

70
00:07:07,540 --> 00:07:08,500
Chan.

71
00:07:08,890 --> 00:07:09,700
I think…

72
00:07:09,740 --> 00:07:10,900
Let’s leave, Key.

73
00:07:18,040 --> 00:07:18,690
Miss Chan.

74
00:07:18,730 --> 00:07:19,760
Don’t follow her.

75
00:07:27,340 --> 00:07:30,030
Bring me all the documents
for today’s meeting.

76
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:32,700
Yes, Mrs. Chanya.

77
00:07:57,030 --> 00:07:58,100
Wait, Chan.

78
00:08:01,850 --> 00:08:02,800
I think…

79
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:05,520
this is getting out of hand.

80
00:08:07,190 --> 00:08:10,600
Your mom will never accept me.

81
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:15,700
Are you giving up?

82
00:08:19,940 --> 00:08:21,720
But I’m putting you in a tight spot.

83
00:08:23,570 --> 00:08:25,170
I don’t want to be selfish

84
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:27,930
and cause a rift between you and your mom.

85
00:08:29,010 --> 00:08:30,520
Then don’t give up.

86
00:08:32,330 --> 00:08:33,730
Don’t leave me.

87
00:08:39,289 --> 00:08:41,500
I will never give up on you.

88
00:08:44,190 --> 00:08:47,970
I believe that we will find a way
to win my mom over

89
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:51,300
as long as we hold onto each other.

90
00:08:58,020 --> 00:08:59,070
I love this.

91
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:02,550
My fiancée is so cool.

92
00:09:03,650 --> 00:09:05,000
This is so touching.

93
00:09:05,620 --> 00:09:07,050
Stop joking around.

94
00:09:08,290 --> 00:09:09,700
I can’t help it.

95
00:09:10,760 --> 00:09:12,100
You are so cool.

96
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:20,470
Promise me.

97
00:09:21,550 --> 00:09:23,700
You will never give up on us.

98
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:27,100
Fine.

99
00:09:28,290 --> 00:09:29,500
Stop nagging me.

100
00:09:31,350 --> 00:09:32,430
I promise.

101
00:09:50,050 --> 00:09:54,240
Thank you for accepting me
into your family.

102
00:09:56,150 --> 00:09:59,700
If Key loves you, we all love you too.

103
00:10:04,370 --> 00:10:09,050
About your mom, what are you going to do?

104
00:10:11,110 --> 00:10:11,900
Yes.

105
00:10:12,280 --> 00:10:14,030
That’s the only thing I’m worried about.

106
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:16,200
If this is not resolved,

107
00:10:16,710 --> 00:10:18,700
you two will never be happy.

108
00:10:19,980 --> 00:10:22,910
About that, Chan and I,

109
00:10:23,580 --> 00:10:26,000
we are counting on a silver bullet
to solve the problem.

110
00:10:26,730 --> 00:10:27,700
A silver bullet?

111
00:10:28,530 --> 00:10:30,200
What is it?

112
00:10:35,350 --> 00:10:36,250
Wait.

113
00:10:36,860 --> 00:10:41,700
Tell me who came up with the plan?

114
00:10:44,110 --> 00:10:45,160
It’s Chan’s plan.

115
00:10:45,980 --> 00:10:47,240
She’s her mom.

116
00:10:48,660 --> 00:10:50,330
Chan knows how to work her way
around her mom.

117
00:10:52,750 --> 00:10:55,700
What is the silver bullet?

118
00:10:59,190 --> 00:11:04,370
It’s someone no one would have expected.

119
00:12:34,950 --> 00:12:37,270
Mom, please take care of Simba for me.

120
00:12:39,990 --> 00:12:41,380
You know I’m allergic to cats.

121
00:12:41,420 --> 00:12:43,120
Why did you leave it with me?

122
00:12:49,610 --> 00:12:51,100
So your name is Simba?

123
00:12:51,670 --> 00:12:52,610
Where are you going?

124
00:12:57,290 --> 00:12:59,550
You will leave a scratch on the chair.

125
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:00,940
Hey.

126
00:13:02,190 --> 00:13:02,900
Hey.

127
00:13:04,520 --> 00:13:07,300
Why are you scratching?
Do you have a skin disease?

128
00:13:09,280 --> 00:13:11,560
Get off the chair.

129
00:13:12,190 --> 00:13:13,100
Do you hear me?

130
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:15,270
Get down to the floor.

131
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:18,940
Get down to the floor.

132
00:13:21,940 --> 00:13:23,310
You understand my words.

133
00:13:24,690 --> 00:13:26,300
Don’t go up to the white sofa.

134
00:13:31,400 --> 00:13:32,200
Hey.

135
00:13:34,970 --> 00:13:36,200
Are you heading to my room?

136
00:13:36,240 --> 00:13:38,080
Don’t go into my room. Come out.

137
00:13:39,490 --> 00:13:41,350
What the hell?!

138
00:13:42,980 --> 00:13:44,270
Gosh!

139
00:13:53,280 --> 00:13:54,090
Meow.

140
00:13:55,080 --> 00:13:55,850
Meow.

141
00:14:00,330 --> 00:14:01,420
Meow, meow.

142
00:14:07,130 --> 00:14:08,100
What is this?

143
00:14:19,290 --> 00:14:22,400
Why did you ask me to meet you
if you are going to say nothing?

144
00:14:26,940 --> 00:14:28,550
I just want you to sit with me.

145
00:14:30,920 --> 00:14:33,070
I’ve been sitting here for almost an hour.

146
00:14:36,920 --> 00:14:42,800
So this is what it feels like
to watch my ex getting married.

147
00:14:47,170 --> 00:14:49,000
Chan probably felt the same back then.

148
00:14:51,070 --> 00:14:52,500
She was in a much worse shape than you.

149
00:14:52,590 --> 00:14:53,900
I saw it with my own eyes.

150
00:14:58,890 --> 00:15:00,700
I guess karma is catching up with me.

151
00:15:03,870 --> 00:15:04,850
You are being extra.

152
00:15:06,640 --> 00:15:07,700
You’re so extra.

153
00:15:13,770 --> 00:15:15,200
I’ll go to the bathroom and be right back.

154
00:15:47,130 --> 00:15:48,570
Do you also drink coffee?

155
00:15:48,950 --> 00:15:50,450
I thought you drank only alcohol.

156
00:16:01,470 --> 00:16:03,560
Your ex is getting married.

157
00:16:04,230 --> 00:16:06,120
Is that why you look dejected?

158
00:16:16,280 --> 00:16:17,200
I know that.

159
00:16:17,680 --> 00:16:18,690
You don’t need to remind me.

160
00:16:19,350 --> 00:16:22,600
I said that because
I want you to face the truth.

161
00:16:25,030 --> 00:16:26,100
Can I ask you something?

162
00:16:26,620 --> 00:16:28,700
How long are you
going to hold on to your ex?

163
00:16:30,470 --> 00:16:31,500
That’s none of your business.

164
00:16:35,190 --> 00:16:38,500
I’m saying this because I mean well.

165
00:16:47,870 --> 00:16:49,400
Can’t I feel sad for a while?

166
00:16:50,510 --> 00:16:52,110
I will get over it eventually.

167
00:16:52,710 --> 00:16:54,500
I still have my pride.

168
00:17:00,870 --> 00:17:02,500
So you are feeling down

169
00:17:03,120 --> 00:17:05,000
because you are trying to get over her?

170
00:17:11,930 --> 00:17:12,849
I like that.

171
00:17:13,250 --> 00:17:14,069
What?

172
00:17:17,460 --> 00:17:20,200
I mean, I like
that you are trying to get over her.

173
00:17:20,380 --> 00:17:21,950
That’s an improvement.

174
00:17:25,849 --> 00:17:27,300
I don’t understand you.

175
00:17:28,020 --> 00:17:29,300
What do you want from me?

176
00:17:29,490 --> 00:17:30,890
Why are you meddling in my business?

177
00:17:31,180 --> 00:17:32,380
I have a lot of free time.

178
00:17:32,710 --> 00:17:34,200
I’m doing this to kill time.

179
00:17:44,130 --> 00:17:45,570
Come on. Get up.

180
00:17:48,160 --> 00:17:49,100
Where are we going?

181
00:17:50,660 --> 00:17:52,000
I’ll give you a reward.

182
00:17:52,420 --> 00:17:53,400
I’ll buy you a meal.

183
00:17:53,970 --> 00:17:54,830
No.

184
00:17:55,310 --> 00:17:56,530
I came here with Phu.

185
00:17:57,510 --> 00:17:58,300
It’s okay.

186
00:17:59,350 --> 00:18:00,130
You can go with her.

187
00:18:03,620 --> 00:18:04,400
Come on.

188
00:18:04,880 --> 00:18:05,600
Get up.

189
00:18:05,860 --> 00:18:07,570
Wear your glasses to look pretty.

190
00:18:09,650 --> 00:18:10,570
I can do it myself.

191
00:18:14,050 --> 00:18:15,430
Come on. Get up.

192
00:18:16,690 --> 00:18:17,810
I can get up by myself.

193
00:18:18,550 --> 00:18:20,380
If you could,
why didn’t you get up sooner?

194
00:18:22,190 --> 00:18:23,100
Your coffee.

195
00:18:24,210 --> 00:18:25,700
-Which way?
-That way.

196
00:18:27,720 --> 00:18:28,520
See you.

197
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:33,300
Jay needs someone like this.

198
00:18:41,960 --> 00:18:44,380
This is where you wanted to take me.

199
00:18:45,870 --> 00:18:48,300
Everyone always celebrates with Moo Krata.

200
00:18:49,470 --> 00:18:51,500
Grilled meat is bad for our health.

201
00:18:52,780 --> 00:18:55,000
You are concerned about your health?

202
00:18:55,450 --> 00:18:56,840
But you get drunk every day.

203
00:18:57,580 --> 00:18:58,570
What an irony.

204
00:19:06,150 --> 00:19:07,080
Can you help fan?

205
00:19:07,110 --> 00:19:08,380
The fire is dying down.

206
00:19:08,800 --> 00:19:09,810
Don’t make me do all the work.

207
00:19:14,460 --> 00:19:16,500
Why do you go through this trouble?

208
00:19:17,570 --> 00:19:19,770
Why didn’t you have them grill it for you?

209
00:19:27,930 --> 00:19:30,200
You need to step out of your comfort zone.

210
00:19:30,910 --> 00:19:33,000
Maybe you’ll get new perspectives.

211
00:19:36,990 --> 00:19:38,870
Stop acting like you’re a life coach.

212
00:19:39,040 --> 00:19:40,160
I’m not falling for it.

213
00:19:44,110 --> 00:19:46,600
Stop acting like you’re a life coach.
I’m not falling for it.

214
00:19:46,640 --> 00:19:48,900
Stop talking and eat it.

215
00:19:53,770 --> 00:19:54,900
Try it.

216
00:19:56,550 --> 00:19:58,770
-It’s burnt.
-Just eat it.

217
00:20:02,590 --> 00:20:04,300
Come on. It won’t kill you.

218
00:20:05,480 --> 00:20:06,400
Try it.

219
00:20:31,540 --> 00:20:32,650
What are you looking at?

220
00:20:33,310 --> 00:20:34,100
What?

221
00:20:35,250 --> 00:20:37,010
I’m looking at you eating. How is it?

222
00:20:37,050 --> 00:20:38,000
Is it good?

223
00:20:40,250 --> 00:20:41,980
It tastes good, doesn’t it?

224
00:20:56,200 --> 00:20:58,310
From the look,
I didn’t think it would taste good.

225
00:21:00,370 --> 00:21:03,900
You little princess, you’ve been living
in your ivory tower for too long.

226
00:21:05,400 --> 00:21:06,300
Hey.

227
00:21:07,010 --> 00:21:08,870
You need to step out
and see the real world.

228
00:21:14,600 --> 00:21:17,090
I just never had a chance to eat it.

229
00:21:18,610 --> 00:21:21,000
If you keep holding on
to the same old things

230
00:21:21,090 --> 00:21:22,700
and cling to the past,

231
00:21:23,080 --> 00:21:24,560
you’ll never know

232
00:21:24,820 --> 00:21:27,600
if there is something better
waiting for you.

233
00:21:31,370 --> 00:21:33,600
Stop expecting your life to be perfect.

234
00:21:34,990 --> 00:21:38,300
Even if your life is not perfect,
it’s not that terrible.

235
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:43,300
Learning to live with your small mistakes

236
00:21:44,320 --> 00:21:45,570
is not a bad thing.

237
00:21:48,520 --> 00:21:49,700
Are you hitting on me?

238
00:21:51,490 --> 00:21:53,500
I’m saying this
because I want to be your friend.

239
00:21:56,120 --> 00:21:57,700
As your new friend,

240
00:21:58,550 --> 00:22:00,670
I want you to stop clinging to the past.

241
00:22:01,880 --> 00:22:03,580
If you keep doing this,

242
00:22:06,620 --> 00:22:08,600
you may lose Chan as a friend.

243
00:22:11,950 --> 00:22:14,900
You need to face the truth and let it go.

244
00:22:17,830 --> 00:22:19,970
Don’t you want to have Chan
in your life as a friend?

245
00:22:21,710 --> 00:22:24,000
Do you really want to lose
a good friend like her?

246
00:22:43,860 --> 00:22:44,700
Here.

247
00:22:45,340 --> 00:22:46,300
I’ll feed you.

248
00:22:50,130 --> 00:22:51,580
Why do I have to eat it?

249
00:22:52,150 --> 00:22:53,980
It’s grilled pork
for our sworn friendship.

250
00:22:54,020 --> 00:22:56,750
This will be an official beginning
of our friendship.

251
00:23:01,960 --> 00:23:02,770
Here.

252
00:23:14,090 --> 00:23:14,970
Come on.

253
00:23:16,650 --> 00:23:17,600
It’s hot.

254
00:23:27,260 --> 00:23:28,100
Here.

255
00:23:32,450 --> 00:23:33,600
Just eat it.

256
00:23:44,410 --> 00:23:45,580
Feed me too.

257
00:23:48,510 --> 00:23:50,430
Come on. I’m hungry.

258
00:23:50,450 --> 00:23:51,950
I haven’t taken a single bite.

259
00:23:52,310 --> 00:23:53,980
You are the only one who is eating.

260
00:24:00,280 --> 00:24:01,650
I like my pork well-done.

261
00:24:15,270 --> 00:24:17,100
That piece is fine.

262
00:24:17,660 --> 00:24:18,700
I can eat it.

263
00:24:20,920 --> 00:24:22,000
Blow it for me.

264
00:24:23,380 --> 00:24:24,900
Come on. It’s hot.

265
00:24:26,820 --> 00:24:28,140
Come on. It’s hot.

266
00:24:37,180 --> 00:24:38,200
Ahh.

267
00:24:44,060 --> 00:24:44,970
It’s delicious.

268
00:24:47,730 --> 00:24:50,700
The new friendship ceremony is complete.

269
00:24:55,030 --> 00:24:56,600
You are strange.

270
00:24:56,810 --> 00:24:58,000
You are strange.

271
00:24:58,140 --> 00:24:59,670
How can you never have eaten
Moo Krata before?

272
00:24:59,710 --> 00:25:03,230
This piece is only for my loved one.

273
00:25:05,990 --> 00:25:07,040
Do you love me?

274
00:25:08,690 --> 00:25:09,800
I love you as a friend.

275
00:25:27,140 --> 00:25:29,100
If you want to smile, just smile.

276
00:25:38,140 --> 00:25:39,200
Let’s do a test.

277
00:25:39,580 --> 00:25:41,560
If you are Thai, you won’t spit it out.

278
00:25:41,710 --> 00:25:42,490
Come on.

279
00:25:44,830 --> 00:25:46,000
I can eat it myself.

280
00:25:54,610 --> 00:25:56,310
If you want to laugh, just laugh.

281
00:25:56,350 --> 00:25:57,490
No need to hold it in.

282
00:25:59,680 --> 00:26:01,400
You look cute when you laugh.

283
00:26:22,550 --> 00:26:23,300
Key.

284
00:26:24,790 --> 00:26:25,700
What?

285
00:26:27,640 --> 00:26:29,000
Why are you making that face?

286
00:26:30,110 --> 00:26:32,000
I was wrong about Mom.

287
00:26:33,660 --> 00:26:34,600
Why?

288
00:26:35,130 --> 00:26:37,670
I don’t know where she took Simba.

289
00:26:38,140 --> 00:26:40,500
I checked the home security camera.
No one is home.

290
00:26:46,740 --> 00:26:47,600
Simba.

291
00:26:48,320 --> 00:26:49,300
Simba.

292
00:26:49,620 --> 00:26:50,870
Simba, where are you?

293
00:26:54,800 --> 00:26:56,520
-Simba.
-Simba.

294
00:26:57,280 --> 00:26:58,780
Simba, Mommy is back.

295
00:26:59,190 --> 00:27:00,200
Where are you?

296
00:27:00,910 --> 00:27:01,800
Simba.

297
00:27:07,210 --> 00:27:09,580
I never thought she would do this.

298
00:27:11,750 --> 00:27:12,960
Calm down, Chan.

299
00:27:13,560 --> 00:27:16,900
I don’t think your mom
would do anything to him.

300
00:27:22,560 --> 00:27:24,300
Do you think…

301
00:27:25,590 --> 00:27:27,200
I’m just afraid that

302
00:27:27,950 --> 00:27:30,200
my mom is so determined to make me give in

303
00:27:32,090 --> 00:27:33,900
that she doesn’t care about anything else.

304
00:27:35,720 --> 00:27:38,000
Do you think she can be that cruel?

305
00:27:40,960 --> 00:27:42,700
When we had problems,

306
00:27:43,600 --> 00:27:45,900
she's never been this drastic.

307
00:27:47,190 --> 00:27:48,500
But this time,

308
00:27:50,110 --> 00:27:52,560
I might be wrong about her.

309
00:28:00,530 --> 00:28:01,400
Mom.

310
00:28:01,720 --> 00:28:03,010
What are you making that face?

311
00:28:03,180 --> 00:28:04,790
Where is Simba?

312
00:28:05,170 --> 00:28:06,250
He’s right here.

313
00:28:07,840 --> 00:28:09,900
Where did you take him?

314
00:28:10,260 --> 00:28:11,690
Why didn’t you tell me first?

315
00:28:11,850 --> 00:28:13,700
I called you,
but you didn’t answer my calls.

316
00:28:13,890 --> 00:28:15,440
I didn’t want to talk to you.

317
00:28:16,450 --> 00:28:18,290
Why did you take Simba with you?

318
00:28:20,090 --> 00:28:21,300
I took him to a groomer.

319
00:28:22,780 --> 00:28:23,560
Huh?

320
00:28:24,120 --> 00:28:27,500
Did you really take him to a groomer?

321
00:28:28,590 --> 00:28:29,800
Yes.

322
00:28:30,630 --> 00:28:32,880
I also bought a new cat tower for him.

323
00:28:33,940 --> 00:28:36,620
I ordered an automatic litter box for him.

324
00:28:36,660 --> 00:28:37,900
It will be delivered soon.

325
00:28:38,320 --> 00:28:41,030
I bought outfits
for the rainy season and winter.

326
00:28:41,470 --> 00:28:42,760
He doesn’t need outfits for summer.

327
00:28:42,960 --> 00:28:44,900
I also bought outfits
for his airport looks.

328
00:28:45,410 --> 00:28:46,920
Can you go get them from my car?

329
00:28:49,740 --> 00:28:50,640
What?

330
00:28:51,420 --> 00:28:53,000
Don’t you hear it?

331
00:28:53,670 --> 00:28:55,970
Go to my car and bring his stuff here.

332
00:28:56,010 --> 00:28:57,200
So he can try his outfits.

333
00:29:00,160 --> 00:29:01,700
Yes. Sure.

334
00:29:10,100 --> 00:29:11,600
Sweetie.

335
00:29:11,950 --> 00:29:12,910
Yes, Mom.

336
00:29:14,270 --> 00:29:15,060
Huh?

337
00:29:17,520 --> 00:29:19,000
I’m not talking to you, Chan.

338
00:29:21,310 --> 00:29:23,240
Right, sweetie?

339
00:29:24,440 --> 00:29:26,380
Are you tired?

340
00:29:28,900 --> 00:29:30,650
Are you no longer allergic to animal fur?

341
00:29:31,760 --> 00:29:33,300
Yes, I still am.

342
00:29:34,080 --> 00:29:37,180
But I’m not allergic to Simba’s fur.

343
00:29:40,300 --> 00:29:41,200
Right?

344
00:29:41,660 --> 00:29:44,300
I’m not allergic to your fur.

345
00:29:44,940 --> 00:29:47,100
You must feel really sleepy.

346
00:29:47,860 --> 00:29:49,180
You turn into jelly.

347
00:29:49,940 --> 00:29:51,500
Okay, okay.

348
00:29:56,390 --> 00:29:58,420
Simba doesn’t seem to want to be with you.

349
00:29:58,460 --> 00:29:59,600
He loves me.

350
00:30:00,040 --> 00:30:01,830
He loves me very much.

351
00:30:01,870 --> 00:30:03,940
He loves and adores me.

352
00:30:03,980 --> 00:30:05,040
Am I right?

353
00:30:07,510 --> 00:30:09,200
What do you want to talk to me about?

354
00:30:09,870 --> 00:30:11,000
It’s about Key.

355
00:30:11,290 --> 00:30:12,760
What else is there to talk about?

356
00:30:13,130 --> 00:30:14,380
About my marriage.

357
00:30:15,630 --> 00:30:17,500
Key is the only one I will marry.

358
00:30:23,250 --> 00:30:25,880
If you want
to have my blessing in marriage,

359
00:30:29,020 --> 00:30:30,500
I have a condition.

360
00:30:34,250 --> 00:30:36,870
Are you going to take Simba from us?

361
00:30:37,400 --> 00:30:38,580
Are you crazy?

362
00:30:39,200 --> 00:30:40,680
What kind of person do you think I am?

363
00:30:43,450 --> 00:30:47,060
What is your condition?

364
00:30:49,040 --> 00:30:51,600
Key must go live with me for one week.

365
00:30:53,440 --> 00:30:55,600
So I can thoroughly evaluate her.

366
00:30:57,920 --> 00:30:58,800
Sure.

367
00:31:01,970 --> 00:31:03,200
That’s not all.

368
00:31:05,230 --> 00:31:10,200
You may want to say no
after hearing my rule.

369
00:31:12,410 --> 00:31:13,450
Rule?

370
00:31:14,670 --> 00:31:15,600
What is it?

371
00:31:18,050 --> 00:31:23,600
You can’t contact Chan at all
while you are living with me.

372
00:31:26,500 --> 00:31:27,580
Why?

373
00:31:28,950 --> 00:31:31,440
Why are you forbidding me to contact her?

374
00:31:31,700 --> 00:31:33,450
If you can’t do it,
then we no longer need to talk.

375
00:31:33,560 --> 00:31:34,600
I can do it.

376
00:31:35,130 --> 00:31:36,240
I’ll do it.

377
00:31:39,190 --> 00:31:40,300
When will we go?

378
00:31:42,140 --> 00:31:43,170
Today.

379
00:31:44,610 --> 00:31:46,000
Right now.

380
00:31:47,120 --> 00:31:47,970
Mom.

381
00:31:48,460 --> 00:31:49,700
I have one more condition.

382
00:31:50,340 --> 00:31:51,500
What is it?

383
00:31:54,160 --> 00:31:55,500
I’ll take Simba with me.

384
00:32:01,480 --> 00:32:02,500
Sure.

385
00:32:04,730 --> 00:32:05,600
No.

386
00:32:06,340 --> 00:32:07,300
I won’t do it.

387
00:32:08,280 --> 00:32:09,650
Then who am I going to be with?

388
00:32:10,230 --> 00:32:13,180
If you feel lonely,
I’ll tell Mam to come and stay with you.

389
00:32:18,590 --> 00:32:21,850
If she doesn’t pass my evaluation,

390
00:32:23,910 --> 00:32:25,280
I won’t allow you two to get married.

391
00:32:28,410 --> 00:32:29,450
I’ll do it.

392
00:32:31,280 --> 00:32:32,810
But I have one condition.

393
00:32:35,940 --> 00:32:36,940
What is it?

394
00:32:39,770 --> 00:32:42,400
Can I call you Mom?

395
00:32:50,170 --> 00:32:51,700
If you pass my evaluation,

396
00:32:54,300 --> 00:32:56,200
I’ll let you call me Mom.

397
00:32:59,610 --> 00:33:01,900
Okay. That’s fair enough.

398
00:33:02,790 --> 00:33:04,760
We have a deal, Mom.

399
00:33:06,880 --> 00:33:08,700
I mean, Madam.

400
00:33:48,220 --> 00:33:49,300
So…

401
00:33:50,670 --> 00:33:52,840
Key is living with your mom,
just the two of them.

402
00:33:53,260 --> 00:33:55,670
Yes, and with the cat.

403
00:33:57,340 --> 00:33:58,500
That’s a good sign.

404
00:33:59,530 --> 00:34:00,500
I know.

405
00:34:01,880 --> 00:34:04,580
But she doesn’t allow me
to talk to Key at all.

406
00:34:04,620 --> 00:34:06,000
That’s what I’m worried about.

407
00:34:08,310 --> 00:34:09,199
Come on.

408
00:34:09,909 --> 00:34:10,900
Hang in there.

409
00:34:12,199 --> 00:34:13,409
To get her blessing in marriage.

410
00:34:14,870 --> 00:34:15,800
Fine.

411
00:34:21,370 --> 00:34:22,300
Right.

412
00:34:24,510 --> 00:34:25,600
About Jay,

413
00:34:27,670 --> 00:34:29,300
you don’t need to worry anymore.

414
00:34:31,600 --> 00:34:33,580
I think she is getting over you.

415
00:34:39,150 --> 00:34:44,500
I hope that you and Jay
can be friends again.

416
00:34:48,520 --> 00:34:50,120
I want us to hang out together.

417
00:34:56,199 --> 00:34:57,000
Yes.

418
00:35:03,010 --> 00:35:04,700
Come on. Let’s go have dinner.

419
00:35:04,860 --> 00:35:05,800
Don’t worry.

420
00:35:06,980 --> 00:35:08,500
I’m sure Key can handle your mom.

421
00:37:31,610 --> 00:37:33,290
Key will be fine, Chan.

422
00:37:35,800 --> 00:37:39,580
I’m sure she can win your mom over.

423
00:37:40,830 --> 00:37:42,100
She is a nice girl.

424
00:37:42,870 --> 00:37:45,650
Everyone who gets to know her
can’t help but fall for her.

425
00:37:50,170 --> 00:37:51,100
Chan.

426
00:37:52,360 --> 00:37:54,400
You must miss her very much, right?

427
00:39:35,300 --> 00:39:36,700
You are holding me tight.

428
00:39:39,270 --> 00:39:40,700
It’s because I miss you.

429
00:39:41,230 --> 00:39:42,670
You need to hold me back.

430
00:39:45,960 --> 00:39:47,900
I miss you too.

431
00:40:03,620 --> 00:40:04,600
How was it?

432
00:40:05,340 --> 00:40:06,900
Did you win my mom over?

433
00:40:09,960 --> 00:40:11,210
Mom?

434
00:40:13,590 --> 00:40:15,100
You call her Mom.

435
00:40:15,510 --> 00:40:17,170
It means that you did it.

436
00:40:19,980 --> 00:40:21,700
Thanks to Simba.

437
00:40:22,450 --> 00:40:24,100
She’s falling hard for him.

438
00:40:25,290 --> 00:40:27,300
If she got upset,
I just handed her the cat.

439
00:40:27,520 --> 00:40:29,520
Soon she would forget it.

440
00:40:31,030 --> 00:40:32,050
Is that so?

441
00:40:35,300 --> 00:40:36,800
Where is Simba?

442
00:40:37,310 --> 00:40:39,100
I miss him too.

443
00:40:39,330 --> 00:40:42,450
Your mom wants him to stay with her
for a few more days.

444
00:40:45,650 --> 00:40:47,920
Be careful.
She might take him to live with her.

445
00:40:51,450 --> 00:40:53,000
I feel bad for her.

446
00:40:53,620 --> 00:40:57,700
She built a cage
so he can enjoy the garden.

447
00:41:01,430 --> 00:41:05,400
I guess we need to adopt another cat.

448
00:41:26,560 --> 00:41:27,750
I miss you so much.

449
00:41:35,580 --> 00:41:37,800
Please stay with me like this every day.

450
00:41:45,280 --> 00:41:47,230
Just waking up to see you,

451
00:41:49,830 --> 00:41:53,600
it already makes me feel happy.

452
00:41:57,810 --> 00:41:58,930
Me too.

453
00:42:01,420 --> 00:42:02,800
My Chan.

454
00:42:26,920 --> 00:42:28,200
I miss you.

455
00:42:44,850 --> 00:42:48,000
Key, where do you want to go
for our honeymoon?

456
00:42:48,720 --> 00:42:51,760
Do you want to go to Europe or Asia?

457
00:42:52,590 --> 00:42:53,800
Anywhere is fine with me.

458
00:42:54,240 --> 00:42:56,410
I can go anywhere
as long as you go with me.

459
00:42:57,380 --> 00:42:59,600
Of course, I will go with you.

460
00:43:05,700 --> 00:43:07,300
In Europe,

461
00:43:08,550 --> 00:43:10,650
which countries have you not visited yet?

462
00:43:11,650 --> 00:43:13,200
Europe?

463
00:43:14,270 --> 00:43:15,850
I have been to several countries.

464
00:43:17,540 --> 00:43:18,930
I traveled a lot.

465
00:43:24,540 --> 00:43:25,840
Who did you travel with?

466
00:43:27,120 --> 00:43:28,080
I…

467
00:43:30,480 --> 00:43:31,640
With Jay?

468
00:43:34,650 --> 00:43:37,700
Can I be jealous?

469
00:43:38,310 --> 00:43:39,500
Yes, you can.

470
00:43:40,650 --> 00:43:42,100
But don’t be mad at me.

471
00:43:43,210 --> 00:43:44,500
Why?

472
00:43:46,190 --> 00:43:47,670
I’m not good at making up.

473
00:43:50,010 --> 00:43:51,500
Then I’ll be mad at you.

474
00:43:52,160 --> 00:43:53,800
So you will get better at making up.

475
00:43:59,970 --> 00:44:01,100
I’m sorry.

476
00:44:02,450 --> 00:44:03,600
I was wrong.

477
00:44:04,840 --> 00:44:06,100
Please don’t be mad at me.

478
00:44:07,520 --> 00:44:08,700
I’m still mad at you.

479
00:44:14,170 --> 00:44:16,330
Please stop being mad at me, pretty girl.

480
00:44:17,530 --> 00:44:18,300
Please.

481
00:44:19,360 --> 00:44:20,960
You need to do more than that.

482
00:44:31,390 --> 00:44:32,800
I’m sorry.

483
00:44:34,490 --> 00:44:35,800
Don’t be mad at me.

484
00:44:37,000 --> 00:44:38,900
From now on,

485
00:44:39,870 --> 00:44:42,300
I’ll take you on lots of vacations.

486
00:44:42,820 --> 00:44:47,900
More than I’ve ever taken anyone else on.

487
00:44:48,560 --> 00:44:49,400
Alright.

488
00:44:53,970 --> 00:44:54,900
You are smiling.

489
00:44:58,190 --> 00:45:00,500
Can you talk to me
like you’re a big sister?

490
00:45:01,560 --> 00:45:03,000
Big sister and little sister.

491
00:45:08,460 --> 00:45:09,920
If I do that,

492
00:45:10,930 --> 00:45:12,330
will you stop being mad at me?

493
00:45:14,630 --> 00:45:15,500
I don’t know.

494
00:45:15,920 --> 00:45:17,300
We’ll have to wait and see.

495
00:45:17,410 --> 00:45:19,100
If I like what I hear.

496
00:45:25,560 --> 00:45:27,100
I’m sorry.

497
00:45:28,900 --> 00:45:30,300
Please don’t be mad at me.

498
00:45:32,480 --> 00:45:33,800
I love you.

499
00:45:41,850 --> 00:45:42,900
Okay.

500
00:45:43,410 --> 00:45:44,760
I’ll let it slide.

501
00:46:03,240 --> 00:46:04,300
You can answer her call.

502
00:46:04,650 --> 00:46:05,600
I’m okay.

503
00:46:08,450 --> 00:46:10,090
Are you really okay with it?

504
00:46:11,580 --> 00:46:12,400
Yes.

505
00:46:13,280 --> 00:46:15,920
I trust you.

506
00:46:30,100 --> 00:46:31,180
Hello, Jay.

507
00:46:41,240 --> 00:46:43,800
Thank you for coming to see me.

508
00:46:45,270 --> 00:46:46,650
I thought you wouldn’t come.

509
00:46:47,560 --> 00:46:49,690
Because you were afraid
that Key would feel uncomfortable.

510
00:46:53,050 --> 00:46:54,400
She is okay with it.

511
00:46:55,330 --> 00:46:56,500
To be honest,

512
00:46:57,490 --> 00:46:59,370
she was the one
who told me to meet you.

513
00:47:00,280 --> 00:47:04,200
So I should thank her

514
00:47:05,420 --> 00:47:07,520
for convincing you to meet me.

515
00:47:12,430 --> 00:47:13,650
I mean it.

516
00:47:14,000 --> 00:47:15,230
I’m not being sarcastic.

517
00:47:20,520 --> 00:47:24,100
You said you had something important
to tell me.

518
00:47:25,840 --> 00:47:26,780
What is it?

519
00:47:34,960 --> 00:47:36,770
The last time we talked,

520
00:47:38,700 --> 00:47:40,200
you told me

521
00:47:43,880 --> 00:47:46,050
you wanted me
to go back to being the old me.

522
00:47:50,870 --> 00:47:52,300
I made up my mind.

523
00:47:53,980 --> 00:47:56,220
I’m going back to being the old Jay.

524
00:48:00,270 --> 00:48:03,450
I’m glad to hear that.

525
00:48:09,270 --> 00:48:11,100
I want to clear the air

526
00:48:12,150 --> 00:48:14,000
for your peace of mind

527
00:48:15,450 --> 00:48:16,930
and mine as well.

528
00:48:22,380 --> 00:48:26,700
All that time,
I was holding on to the past.

529
00:48:28,740 --> 00:48:31,070
I did everything to get you back.

530
00:48:34,900 --> 00:48:36,860
I put you in a difficult position.

531
00:48:38,410 --> 00:48:40,200
It was also painful for me.

532
00:48:44,020 --> 00:48:45,400
Now I know…

533
00:48:47,100 --> 00:48:48,870
what the right thing is.

534
00:48:51,940 --> 00:48:53,800
The right thing is…

535
00:48:54,650 --> 00:48:56,150
I have to let you go.

536
00:48:57,750 --> 00:48:59,700
So that I can start a new chapter.

537
00:49:12,030 --> 00:49:13,200
I’m sorry…

538
00:49:15,330 --> 00:49:17,200
for everything I did to you.

539
00:49:22,730 --> 00:49:28,000
Both back then and now.

540
00:49:32,490 --> 00:49:34,300
You don’t need to forgive me.

541
00:49:37,600 --> 00:49:38,380
But…

542
00:49:42,110 --> 00:49:44,170
will you accept my apology?

543
00:49:57,680 --> 00:49:58,870
I forgive you.

544
00:50:15,350 --> 00:50:16,300
So…

545
00:50:20,120 --> 00:50:24,900
you and I,

546
00:50:26,440 --> 00:50:28,200
can we still be friends?

547
00:50:30,390 --> 00:50:31,400
Sure.

548
00:50:34,410 --> 00:50:36,030
But it will take some time.

549
00:50:39,580 --> 00:50:40,600
I get it.

550
00:50:49,880 --> 00:50:51,570
I have nothing more to say to you.

551
00:50:53,820 --> 00:50:54,800
I’m leaving.

552
00:51:00,580 --> 00:51:01,300
Bye.

553
00:51:03,460 --> 00:51:04,400
Bye.

554
00:51:47,240 --> 00:51:50,970
6 MONTHS LATER

555
00:52:07,830 --> 00:52:09,300
Whose bride is this?

556
00:52:09,900 --> 00:52:11,050
You look beautiful.

557
00:52:13,170 --> 00:52:15,400
My bride is also beautiful.

558
00:52:17,310 --> 00:52:20,880
Chan, you look so beautiful today
that I want to kiss you.

559
